+   "source": [
+    "# Data Augmentation Visualization for fMRI Flat Maps\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This notebook visualizes different data augmentation techniques for fMRI flat map data.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For each augmentation type, we display:\n",
+    "- **4 different data samples** (rows)\n",
+    "- **5 columns**: original + 4 random augmentation samples\n",
+    "- **Single frame** from multi-frame clips for clarity\n",
+    "\n",
+    "## Augmentation Types\n",
+    "\n",
+    "1. **Random Crop (Weak)**: scale=[0.8, 1.0], ratio=[2.5, 2.5]\n",
+    "2. **Random Crop (Moderate)**: scale=[0.25, 1.0], ratio=[2.0, 3.125]\n",
+    "3. **Color Jitter**: brightness, contrast adjustments (single channel)\n",
+    "4. **Gaussian Noise**: additive Gaussian noise"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 1,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import torch\n",
+    "import numpy as np\n",
+    "from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n",
+    "from huggingface_hub import hf_hub_download\n",
+    "import torchvision.transforms.v2 as v2\n",
+    "import torchvision.transforms.v2.functional as TF\n",
+    "\n",
+    "from data.flat_data import make_flat_wds_dataset, make_flat_transform\n",
+    "from flat_mae.visualization import FC_CMAP"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 2,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
